        "original_id": "f5291fb1-b62a-5a92-bd2f-2d69aa4a4960",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Idrissa Ouédraogo, Jerry Paris\n- Products: Yaaba\n- Places: Banfora, Upper Volta, Burkina Faso, Africa\n- Roles: film director, actor, director\n- Topics: African film, rural and city conflict, tradition and modernity\n\nFacts:\n- Jerry Paris was born on July 25, 1925, and he was an American actor and director.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo was born on 21 January 1954 in Banfora, Upper Volta.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo was a film director from Burkina Faso who made films set within Africa.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo often explored conflicts between rural and city life and between tradition and modernity in his films.\n- Yaaba is a 1989 Burkinabé drama film.\n- Idrissa Ouédraogo wrote, produced, and directed Yaaba.\n- Jerry Paris died on March 31, 1986.\n- Jerry Paris was best known for playing Jerry Helper, the dentist and next-door neighbor of Rob and Laura Petrie, on The Dick Van Dyke Show.",
